## Additional terms for the Vibe Appliance

**What the appliance is.** The Vibe Appliance is a meta-installer. It
composes container images published by the Vibe product family and by
third parties; it does not include their source. Each composed
component is licensed separately by its own publisher, and nothing in
these terms grants any license to those components. See
docs/CONNECT_BLOCKED.md for the family license inventory.

**Third-party components.** The appliance pulls and runs images
including Caddy (Apache-2.0), PostgreSQL / ParadeDB (PostgreSQL
License / AGPL-3.0), Redis (RSALv2 / SSPL), HAProxy (GPLv2),
Portainer CE (zlib), Duplicati (LGPL-2.1), Cockpit (LGPL-2.1),
cloudflared (Apache-2.0) and Tailscale (BSD-3-Clause). Each remains
under its own license, which travels with the image.

**No warranty of compliance.** The appliance installs and operates
software that a firm may rely on for regulatory obligations. It does
not guarantee compliance, prevent breaches, or constitute legal
advice. The firm retains responsibility for its own information
security program and for every regulatory determination it makes.
